#: ../../source/docs/quiktune.rst:5 798ed90e40d34bbcb3f1fa5e64924be7
msgid "QuikTune"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quiktune.rst:10 bfd26fe653ef47739300592d0fc5be20
msgid ""
"The `VTOL QuikTune "
"<https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/Copter-4.5/libraries/AP_Scripting/applets/VTOL-"
"quicktune.md>`__ Lua script simplifies the process of finding a good tune "
"for a multicopter's attitude control parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quiktune.rst:12 7f27a975f6d94ee6a9c6188d5e413694
msgid ""
"The script slowly increases the relevant gains until it detects an "
"oscillation.  It then reduces the gains by 60% and moves onto the next gain."
" Once all the gains have been tuned the tune completes and the user can "
"decide to save or discard the new gains."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quiktune.rst:15 94939a228afe4e94830f92efe5861ba9
msgid ""
"be sure that you have prepared the vehicle for tuning by setting up "
"parameters discussed here: :ref:`setting-up-for-tuning`. Also to assure the "
"best tune, setup the noise notch filtering, see :ref:`common-imu-notch-"
"filtering`. You may run QuickTune without this step to obtain initial fine "
"tune, see :ref:`ac_rollpitchtuning` if the vehicle cant do an initial hover "
"stably. Then setup the filters and retune for best results."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quiktune.rst:17 1325d8592e9a432c9c41f7082e9aaf93
msgid "The script attempts to tune all these parameters (in the given order)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quiktune.rst:19 51f32807f484449e8f4d8c04efb9676b
msgid ":ref:`ATC_RAT_RLL_D<ATC_RAT_RLL_D__AC_AttitudeControl_Multi>`"
msgstr ""

